#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - libfirm 1.22.0 perl build generators need
# PERL_USE_UNSAFE_INC on Perl >= 5.26
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-libfirm-1.22.0-perl-unsafe-inc
trigger_tool:           make|perl
phase:                  build
error_signature:        "'\\.' is no longer in @INC|did you mean do \"./|generate_emitter\.pl.*Fatal error|@INC.*generate_regalloc"
severity:               2
category:               build-tool, perl, compat, portability, build-system
match_keywords:         perl, @INC, PERL_USE_UNSAFE_INC, generate_emitter, code generator, Perl 5.26, relative do, libfirm
title:                  Perl >= 5.26 removed '.' from @INC — build-time perl generators that `do` a relative spec path fail

root_cause:             Perl 5.26 removed the current directory '.' from @INC for
                        security reasons. Upstream build generators written for older
                        Perl use `do $specfile` (or `require`) with a path relative to
                        the invoking script (e.g. ir/be/scripts/generate_emitter.pl
                        does 'ir/be/amd64/amd64_spec.pl'). On Perl >= 5.26 this fails
                        with "'.' is no longer in @INC; did you mean do
                        './ir/be/amd64/amd64_spec.pl'?" and the make target dies.

rec_approach:           export PERL_USE_UNSAFE_INC=1 in the build environment
                        (restores '.' to @INC for legacy scripts). Preferred over
                        patching every 'do' call site: it is one environment line in
                        the recipe, and it does not alter generated output.

verification_cmd:       PERL_USE_UNSAFE_INC=1 make -j1 CC=clang LINK=clang
verification:           libfirm 1.22.0: after exporting PERL_USE_UNSAFE_INC=1 the
                        previously failing targets build/gen/ir/be/*/gen_*_emitter.h
                        were generated and `make` completed (exit 0); without it make
                        fails at generate_emitter.pl line 23 "couldn't do
                        ir/be/amd64/amd64_spec.pl".

affected_scope:         Any C/C++ project whose Makefile invokes a vendored Perl
                        code generator that loads sibling spec files with relative
                        paths, on hosts with Perl >= 5.26 (OHOS PC, newer distros).

forbid_1_pattern:       patch.*perl.*script.*absolute path|sed.*generate_emitter.*@INC
forbid_1_reason:        Rewriting every 'do' call site is invasive and unnecessary; the
                        environment variable is the minimal reversible fix.
forbid_1_consequence:   Larger patches that are hard to review and conflict-prone.

similar_to:             [E116, E155]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

